{{ if $values }}Environment: ${ALERT_ENVIRONMENT}
What was reused: {{ .Labels.what }}
Times in the last 5 minutes: {{ printf "%.0f" .Values.B.Value }}

The grant is already ended; its user must connect the app again. The grant-ended event next to the reuse names the client, the grant and the user by pseudonym. Reuse across many users of one app is a bug in that app: tell its maker. Reuse on one user's grant, by an app that otherwise works, is a copied token: ask the user where the app runs, and if a token may have leaked, revoke their sessions, which ends all their grants (the realm-auth skill). Find the rows a pseudonym stands for with the SQL in the oauth-provider skill's Alerts section; the dashboard shows the events around it.{{ else }}Environment: ${ALERT_ENVIRONMENT}

